editor {"type": "text", "doc": "m", "text": "# Marker test\n\nAn inserted paragraph pushing everything down.\n\nAnother inserted one.\n\nA paragraph of several lines. The cursor marker should be a bar in the left margin next to this whole block,\nwith a small tick at the line the cursor is on, which is the third line of this paragraph, so the\ntick sits about two thirds down the bar. Some more words to make it wrap properly over the column\nwidth of the reading area.\n\n```rust\n    let value_1 = compute(1); // line 1 of the code\n    let value_2 = compute(2); // line 2 of the code\n    let value_3 = compute(3); // line 3 of the code\n    let value_4 = compute(4); // line 4 of the code\n    let value_5 = compute(5); // line 5 of the code\n    let value_6 = compute(6); // line 6 of the code\n    let value_7 = compute(7); // line 7 of the code\n    let value_8 = compute(8); // line 8 of the code\n    let value_9 = compute(9); // line 9 of the code\n    let value_10 = compute(10); // line 10 of the code\n    let value_11 = compute(11); // line 11 of the code\n    let value_12 = compute(12); // line 12 of the code\n    let value_13 = compute(13); // line 13 of the code\n    let value_14 = compute(14); // line 14 of the code\n    let value_15 = compute(15); // line 15 of the code\n    let value_16 = compute(16); // line 16 of the code\n```\n\nFinal paragraph, one line.\n\n"}
